  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent-description; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a person in a flowing white garment, appearing angelic or ethereal, floating amidst clouds and falling petals, evoking a sense of peace, purity, or divine reward. The text overlay reads 'when you haven't stolen anything in a week.' The overall intent is to humorously and ironically suggest that abstaining from theft for a week is so virtuous or rare that it merits angelic status. This is a self-deprecating or satirical meme that uses the juxtaposition of a heavenly image with a mundane, morally ambiguous act (theft) to create comedic contrast. There is no toxicity present; the meme does not target any specific group or individual based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The intent is purely comedic and relies on the absurdity of equating a short period of non-theft with angelic reward, without any harmful or discriminatory implications.",
